{"content":"To answer your question directly: Whether two people are cousins depends on their family relationships. Cousins are typically defined as the children of two siblings or second cousins, the children of two first cousins.\n\nHere’s a more detailed explanation:\n\n1. **First Cousins**: These are the children of two siblings. For example, if Alice and Bob are siblings, and Carol and Dave are siblings, then Alice and Carol are first cousins, and Alice and Dave are also first cousins.\n\n2. **Second Cousins**: These are the children of two first cousins. For example, if Alice and Carol are first cousins (children of siblings), and then Alice and Dave are also first cousins (children of siblings), then Alice and Dave are second cousins.\n\nIf the individuals in question are the children of siblings, they are first cousins. If they are the children of first cousins, they are second cousins, and so on.\n\nIf you can provide more specific details about the family relationships, I can give a more precise answer!","level":"info","message":"Inference Client response:","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[]}
